.TH CYAML_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_destroy \- recursively free a DOM tree and null the handle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml_destroy(node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
If node is non-NULL, recursively frees the entire DOM subtree rooted at
node using each node's stored allocator, then sets node to NULL.

List children, dictionary values, and string copies are all freed
recursively.  Double-freeing a destroyed handle is safe because the
macro nulls the variable first.

To destroy a tree without nulling the pointer, call __cyaml_destroy()
directly.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  cyaml variable to destroy.  The variable itself is set to NULL.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyaml root = cyaml_parse("a: 1\en", NULL);
/* ... use root ... */
cyaml_destroy(root);   /* root is now NULL */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare_scoped (3),
.BR __cyaml_destroy (3)
